   GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1.2}}, "Rows" -> {{0.6}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"f59e296c-aaff-423c-a9ab-5315dc0aaabd"],

Cell["\<\
Two causes, and only two. Inside a loop, the rule reads nothing: with for o \
in objs: if a: return s as the only success, the action needs the loop to run \
and a to hold, but the rule gives up both to stay sound when the loop runs \
zero times. In real domains such tests also read loop variables that no trace \
binds, so they could not have been evaluated. Where a test repeats, the rule \
treats each if as independent: in if a: return s else: (if a: pass else: \
return False), the second test of a is decided by the first, so a is \
necessary, but no if requires it on every path. Round 00 found its own \
precision gap in the same place, where a leaf repeats.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e6230315-86c3-4d91-92e1-1f4c7432ca4e"],

Cell["R5. The code computes the model", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d09ac068-12b9-4236-9bec-bd15d118400a"],

Cell["\<\
The proof is about the model, so this checks that guards.py computes exactly \
what the model predicts, for both readings, on every program of R3. \
scripts/cf_agree.py renders each program as a Python action, runs \
extract_action_guards from 0.1.1 (dc3f852^) and from dc3f852, maps each atom \
back to its if, and compares.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a0cfaa0a-d5e3-40a9-9cdf-33c0785085d4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"json", "=", 
      RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
        "$TemporaryDirectory", ",", "\"\<guard_cf_programs.json\>\""}], "}"}],
        "]"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"old", "=", 
      RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
        "$TemporaryDirectory", ",", "\"\<guard_cf_old_guards.py\>\""}], "}"}],
        "]"}]}], ",", "res"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Export", "[", 
     RowBox[{"json", ",", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Association", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\"\<prog\>\"", "\[Rule]", 
            RowBox[{"toJ", "[", "#1", "]"}]}], ",", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<old\>\"", "\[Rule]", 
            RowBox[{"oldReq", "[", "#1", "]"}]}], ",", 
           RowBox[{"\"\<new\>\"", "\[Rule]", 
            RowBox[{"newReq", "[", "#1", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], "&"}], ")"}], "/@",
        "progs"}], ",", "\"\<RawJSON\>\"", ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Compact\>\"", "\[Rule]", "True"}]}], "]"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"WriteString", "[", 
     RowBox[{"old", ",", 
      RowBox[{"RunProcess", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<git\>\"", ",", "\"\<-C\>\"", ",", "$repo", 
          ",", "\"\<show\>\"", 
          ",", "\"\<dc3f852^:packages/gtpyhop-diagnostics/src/gtpyhop/\
diagnostics/guards.py\>\""}], "}"}], ",", "\"\<StandardOutput\>\""}], "]"}]}],
      "]"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"Close", "[", "old", "]"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"res", "=", 
     RowBox[{"RunProcess", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"\"\<python3\>\"", ",", "\"\<-S\>\"", ",", 
        RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
          "$here", ",", "\"\<scripts\>\"", ",", "\"\<cf_agree.py\>\""}], 
          "}"}], "]"}], ",", "old", ",", 
        RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
          "$repo", ",", "\"\<packages\>\"", ",", "\"\<gtpyhop-diagnostics\>\"",
            ",", "\"\<src\>\"", ",", "\"\<gtpyhop\>\"", 
           ",", "\"\<diagnostics\>\"", ",", "\"\<guards.py\>\""}], "}"}], 
         "]"}], ",", "json"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"DeleteFile", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"json", ",", "old"}], "}"}], "]"}], ";", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"res", "[", "\"\<ExitCode\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"StringTrim", "[", 
       RowBox[{"res", "[", "\"\<StandardOutput\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}], 
     "}"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"5c7a87fb-ac16-448e-b713-\
ca5de0624d44"],

