Cell["\<\
Caption: the ast.walk reading extracts unsound atoms (red) and the path-aware \
one none. The grey shrinks too, but most of the sound atoms it drops are \
vacuous, from bodies that can never succeed (R4).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9b7f5094-b89b-4f0a-81de-f9ceea84a2b7"],

Cell["Contradictions & Surprises", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2a24b4d9-785c-498a-bd5a-7a87f51c37a7"],

Cell["\<\
Round 00 said a_submit_job's launcher != 'mpirun' is reported as failed. It \
is extracted, but it reads a local the evaluator cannot bind, so it lands as \
unevaluated. The false blocker that is actually named is its sibling \
processes_per_node < 1 (R6).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"091d5443-4f26-49eb-adc4-c8cc7ba84b96"],

Cell["\<\
The upper-bound script undercounted. It missed bio_opentrons \
a_open_thermocycler_lid, whose idempotent early return state 0.1.1 read as \
requiring the lid already open, and the else branch of rikyu_hpc a_fs_tail.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"e25bd1b2-5d9a-4907-93c6-48f8c07cdca0"],

Cell["Steering Questions", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"81ce3955-c5f9-4c0a-a974-b6096f62b6a1"],

Cell["\<\
[now] File the control-flow issue (ISSUE_DRAFT.md) with dc3f852 as its fix, \
then release as a patch?\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"6844fbb6-cfa8-4668-8b80-63071036b090"],

Cell["\<\
[next run] Precision: conjoin a nested bail's enclosing test into one atom \
(if C: if T: return False \[RightArrow] not (C and T)), and turn a loop bail \
into all(...) over the loop. Both add atoms, so both are features rather than \
fixes.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"025e787d-25af-44b1-b243-8e40eea377b7"],

Cell["Pointers", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"b160f31e-3546-4eda-9493-c162f7e04556"],

Cell["\<\
Commit dc3f852 (fix), on top of b0115ef (round 00 of diagnostics_guard_nnf)\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"83046986-6751-4a2f-bcf3-d82c5c2bab48"],

Cell["\<\
tools/diagnostics_guard_check.py: 14 cases, including the executed \
control-flow property case, in checks.yml\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d81da12c-2241-4dbc-9177-a5c0b209865a"],

Cell["\<\
scripts/cf_agree.py next to this notebook (R5); \
diagnostics_guard_nnf/scripts/ for the measurements\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"fa59cb1b-28b3-48dc-9000-e4e4e753307e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Appendix: definitions (initialization cells)", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0b99f221-5bbb-442d-b3e3-9c484e5f9552"],

Cell["\<\
Inert syntax ok, bail, eff, if[id, t, A, B], loop[id, A] over tests p, q, r. \
sem is the success condition, an mirrors guards._required_on_success, oldPol \
the per-if reading both versions share, oldReq the 0.1.1 result and newReq \
the dc3f852 result. The notebook has its own context (CellContext -> \
Notebook).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"072eb9eb-c0a6-4fc7-963c-459243aa42bf"],

